    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0293" n="187" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg187"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <hi rendition="#italic"><date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1906-05-03">May 3,
                        1906</date></hi>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(States that he is informed by the Chinese Government that it will be ready in a
                    few days to select at Antung a suitable locality for <pb facs="0294" n="188"
                        xml:id="pg188"/> an international settlement and otherwise comply with
                    article 12 of our treaty of 1903. The Japanese minister says that he is
                    authorized by his Government to cooperate with us in the matter as well as for a
                    similar object later on at Mukden, and that he will send a duly empowered agent
                    to Antung to discuss and agree on these matters jointly with representatives of
                    America and China. Mr. Rockhill inquires whether he may instruct the
                    consul-general at Newchwang to go to Antung as soon as his presence is needed
                    there and duly empower him to agree to the site of the settlement as well as the
                    regulations, subject to the department’s approval. States that the settlement of
                    these questions at Mukden will take place on or after June 1, and that some one
                    must be sent there for the same object by the American Government.)</p>
            </div>
